      "key_disallowances": [
        {
          "component": "employee_cost",
          "claimed": 54.54,
          "approved": 27.82,
          "kserc_reasoning": "As per the Tariff Regulations, 2021, the licensee shall be allowed to recover the operation and maintenance expenses as per the norms specified in Annexure-7 of Tariff Regulations 2021 for each financial year of the Control Period. ... Considering the above, the Commission hereby approves the employee cost of Rs. 27.82 lakh for the year 2022-23 as per the norm after adjusting actual inflation."
        },
        {
          "component": "power_purchase_cost",
          "claimed": 4652.88,
          "approved": 4606.04,
          "kserc_reasoning": "As per the Tariff Regulations 2021, if the actual distribution loss is higher than the approved level of distribution loss, then the quantum of power purchased corresponding to the excess distribution loss shall be disallowed at the average cost of power purchase. Accordingly, the power purchase cost based on the approved distribution loss of 3.45% for the year 2022-23 is as shown below."
        },
        {
          "component": "section3_1_duty",
          "claimed": 36.98,
          "approved": 0.0,
          "kserc_reasoning": "The Commission examined the submission of the licensee and observed that, the licensee has booked Rs. 36.98 lakh towards Electricity Duty for the year 2022-23. The Commission in the previous Orders had stated that duty under Section 3 cannot be passed on to the consumers in view of the statutory provisions of the Kerala Electricity Duty Act, 1963. Hence the same is disallowed."
        },
        {
          "component": "depreciation",
          "claimed": 162.45,
          "approved": 75.43,
          "kserc_reasoning": "Accordingly, the Commission hereby approves depreciation of Rs.94.17 lakh for the year 2019-20, Rs. 96.59 for the year 2020-21 Rs.75.50 lakh for the year 2021-22 and Rs.75.43 lakh for the year 2022-23 as per the revised calculation as shown above. ... Accordingly, the Commission hereby claws back Rs. 162.56 lakh as excess amount of depreciation provisionally approved in previous years."
        }
      ],
