      "key_disallowances": [
        {
          "component": "employee_cost",
          "claimed": 29.86,
          "approved": 25.07,
          "kserc_reasoning": "The major heads under employee expense are basic salary, DA, other allowances etc. The Commission analysed the details submitted by the licensee and is of the view that, O&M expense being a controllable expense may be limited to the approved norms. Accordingly, the Commission hereby approves the employee expenses of Rs.25.07 lakh based on actual inflation rate for the year 2024-25 as worked out in Table 13 as against the licensee’s claim of Rs.29.86 lakh."
        },
        {
          "component": "repair_maintenance",
          "claimed": 58.3,
          "approved": 34.13,
          "kserc_reasoning": "During the hearing with regard to the onetime expenditure incurred for the replacement of EHT bushing (220 KV grade) at Phase II and for LA at Cherthala installations, the Commission was of the opinion that it shall be treated as capital expenditure instead of claiming it under the head Repair and Maintenance expense. The licensee vide clarifications dated 21.01.2026 treating it as asset addition and the eligible depreciation for the replacement of the EHT bushing and LA will be claimed in the ensuing year as prior period depreciation. Therefore, after analysing the details the Commission hereby approves Rs.7.69 lakh (Excluding the onetime expense of Rs.8.80 lakh for replacement of EHT bushing and Rs.2.79 lakh for Replacement of LA) as onetime expenditure for the year 2024-25."
        },
        {
          "component": "admin_general",
          "claimed": 10.06,
          "approved": 7.35,
          "kserc_reasoning": "The Commission examined the submissions by the licensee as well as the explanations given in the hearing and noted that Energy audit fee can be considered as an additional item which was not reckoned at the time of arriving at the norms. Therefore, the Commission approves Rs.2.24 lakh as Energy Audit fee under A&G Expenses. Considering Para 28 of this Order, the Commission has already approved Rs.5.11 lakh as A&G Expenses based on actual inflation rate for the year 2024-25 which aligns with the approved norms as per Tariff Regulations 2021. Therefore, Commission hereby approves an amount of Rs.7.35 lakh (Rs.5.11 lakh+ Rs.2.24 lakh) as the A&G expenses for the year 2024-25."
        }
